An :IF missing its :ENDIF inside the first of two procedures. The
recovery path of unclosed_block reports the :IF when the :ENDPROC is
reached, and the :ENDPROC still closes the procedure, so the second
procedure is judged on its own and nothing cascades into it
(diag.unclosed_block recovery; diag.mismatched_block_end must not fire).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE ApplyDiscount;
	:PARAMETERS nAmount;
	:DECLARE nResult;
	nResult := nAmount;
	:IF nAmount > 100;
		nResult := nAmount * 0.9;
	:RETURN nResult;
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE RoundAmount;
	:PARAMETERS nAmount;
	:IF nAmount < 0;
		:RETURN 0;
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN Round(nAmount, 2);
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE ApplyDiscount;
	:PARAMETERS nAmount;
	:DECLARE nResult;
	nResult := nAmount;
	:IF nAmount > 100;
		nResult := nAmount * 0.9;
		:RETURN nResult;
	:ENDPROC;

	:PROCEDURE RoundAmount;
		:PARAMETERS nAmount;
		:IF nAmount < 0;
			:RETURN 0;
		:ENDIF;
		:RETURN Round(nAmount, 2);
	:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
5:2-5:5 error unclosed_block: Unclosed ':IF' - expected ':ENDIF'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
5:2-5:5 error unclosed_block: Unclosed ':IF' - expected ':ENDIF'
